From abeef58ff899175e804d82866dbe2ec10ef8e5b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noor Masud <noor.masud@get-licensed.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:51:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Railway build: drop npm ci from buildCommand, move tsc to
 dependencies

Two build-phase failures:

1. railway.json ran "npm ci && npm run build" as the build command. Nixpacks
   already installs in its own phase and mounts a cache at node_modules/.cache;
   npm ci then tried to remove node_modules underneath that mount, failing with
   EBUSY. The build phase should only build.

2. Railway installs with dev dependencies omitted, so typescript was absent and
   tsc would not resolve even once EBUSY was fixed. typescript and the @types
   packages move to dependencies; tsx stays in devDependencies since only the
   offline replay harness needs it.

Verified against a clean NODE_ENV=production npm ci --omit=dev, which now
builds dist/index.js and serves /health.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018s7bzXTVT4wfbEeWDHtGmA
